2|Death’s Door: Reduced to zero hp. If other PCs, hirelings, etc are with them, the PC makes a Death save at advantage. Otherwise the body is lost and they die.
3-4|Injured: Roll [[1d20]] on the Injuries & Setbacks table.
5|Diseased: Roll [[1d12]] on the Diseases table.
6|Poisoned: Poisoned by a random plant, animal, etc. Roll [[1d12]] on the Poison table (p.226) but effects last until you receive an Antitoxin treatment, or one month passes, whichever occurs first (excluding hp damage).
7|Battle: Lose [[2d10]] hp. If reduced to zero hp apply Death’s Door above.
8|Lost Gear: Randomly use up or lose one piece of gear. Roll [[1d6]] (i-ii) Battle Gear, (iii-vi) Pack Gear. Reroll magic items.
9|Animal Death: [[1d4]] horses, pets, or other animals are lost. Beast companions are reduced to zero hp instead.
10|Hireling Death: A hireling or NPC is lost. Henchmen are reduced to zero hp instead. For a much loved hireling, the GM might Consult the Bones to see if they roll on the Injuries & Setbacks table instead.
11-12|Bonus Loot!: You find hidden treasure or an empty lair. Roll [[1d6]] (i) Carry Loot B, (ii) Valuables A, (iii) Trinket or Curio, (iv) Minor Charm, (v) Scroll, (vi) Potion.